# The harvested shards are large and re-derivable from sources.json + the web.
# Keep the registry; leave the bulk out of git until there is a decision about
# where this data actually lives (see README).
#
# This used to say "keep the registry, the resume state and the reports". The
# resume state turned out to be 592 files and ~50 MB, rewritten on every harvest
# run and useless on any machine but the one that produced it, and the reports
# are regenerated by `report.mjs` from the shards. Both are excluded from the
# ROOT .gitignore now, which is where the reasoning lives — this file is only
# consulted for paths under `corpus/`, and the same rules apply to
# `recipeData/`.
recipes/*.jsonl
_state/discovered/*.json
_state/done/*.log
index.jsonl

# Generated by `tool/corpus_import.dart gen` — 71 MB for a 21,000-recipe tier,
# and re-derivable from the shards in seconds. The committed artifact is the
# TOOL, not its output (Phase 35c).
_import/
_import_*/
